Package: Fonology
Type: Package
Title: Phonological Analysis in R
Version: 1.7.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = c("Guilherme", "D."), family = "Garcia",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "guilherme.garcia@lli.ulaval.ca",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1412-3856")),
    person(family = "Wiktionary contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "Spanish and Italian lexicons and curated Portuguese corrections"),
    person(family = "Lexique 4 contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "French pronunciation lexicon")
  )
Maintainer: Guilherme D. Garcia <guilherme.garcia@lli.ulaval.ca>
Description: A collection of tools for phonological analysis, with primary support for Portuguese, Spanish, French, and Italian, plus PSL-backed Portuguese, Lexique-backed French, and CMU-backed English transcription with user-correctable overrides and heuristic fallback for out-of-vocabulary forms. Functions include grapheme-to-phoneme conversion with syllabification and stress assignment, sonority dispersion calculation, minimal matrices for natural classes given a set of features, maxent models, and more.
